From feb4e175fec7fddaabf6f748de095f8ef4074185 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Starbite build <build@starbite.invalid>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:47:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] panfrost, d3d10umd: a Direct3D depth bias is in steps of
 the depth buffer, not doubled

T82, every pass on our driver: test_depth_bias fails 437 of 40106 checks,
all of them the DepthBias part with D24_UNORM_S8_UINT and D16_UNORM, and in
every one the depth read back is the expected value with twice the bias
(checked for all 437 lines: clamp(2 * bias) reproduces what was read; the
D32_FLOAT cases pass).

Panfrost multiplies offset_units by two for a fixed-point depth buffer (its
minimum resolvable difference; GL leaves that to the implementation).
Direct3D 10 defines the unit as one step of the buffer, which is what the
hardware unit turns out to be. pipe_rasterizer_state gets
sb_offset_units_exact; d3d10umd sets it, Panfrost then passes the units on
unscaled. Other frontends keep the factor.

Compiled only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_cmdstream.c  | 16 +++++++++++++---
 src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Rasterizer.cpp |  3 +++
 src/gallium/include/pipe/p_state.h            |  9 +++++++++
 3 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_cmdstream.c b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_cmdstream.c
index 5a7e542..b2b14c6 100644
