Subject: [PATCH 6/8] d3d10umd: a render target view of a buffer is created
 empty instead of removing the device

T82 pass N, d3d11 test_create_rendertarget_view: CreateRenderTargetView on a
buffer (D3D11_RTV_DIMENSION_BUFFER, legal) returns DXGI_ERROR_DEVICE_REMOVED
and the test then crashes on the view it did not get. The driver answered
SetError(E_NOTIMPL) ("Render target view into buffer!"), which the runtime
treats as the loss of the device. It also left the view object as the
runtime allocated it, which DestroyRenderTargetView then dropped a reference
through, and kept one reference to the buffer for good.

No gallium driver here renders into a buffer, so the view is created with no
surface: bound, it is an empty render target slot; clearing it does nothing;
what is drawn into it is lost (one log line says so). The unknown-dimension
branches of both view creations leave a clean object the same way.

