From e92ebbf244d46156f65aa33694df4439d8a464ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Starbite build <build@starbite.invalid>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:51:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] panfrost: the stream output and geometry capture vertex
 variants follow the integer vertex elements

T82 pass N, d3d11 test_vertex_id: the stream output of a vertex shader whose
input is an R32_UINT element holds 0x3f800000, 0x40000000, ... where the ids
1, 2, ... are expected: the element converted to float.

A vertex shader variant is keyed on which vertex elements are pure integers
(sb_retype_int_attribs loads those raw). The two variants kept outside the
variant list were not: the transform feedback one (vs->xfb) is compiled when
the shader is created and the geometry capture one (vs->gs_capture, gsemu)
at its first draw, both for "no integer element". They are now compiled
again when the elements bound at a draw differ from the ones they were made
for (panfrost_sb_special_vs_variant). For that the transform feedback key
alone has to select the transform feedback lowering, since the shader it is
made from has had has_transform_feedback_varyings cleared by then.

The other failures of the test (indexed draws captured only through the
geometry path) are not touched. Compiled only.

